---
const firstParagraph = "I wanted cinematic content for my fashion brand, with cameras, locations, sets, the whole thing.";
---

<section id="why" class="relative bg-muted px-6 py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-muted-foreground">
      // frame 072 / why I'm building this
    </p>

    <h2
      class="m-0 text-[clamp(30px,4vw,46px)] font-medium leading-[1.12] tracking-[var(--tracking-tight)] text-foreground"
    >
      I fell in love with the craft.
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-5">
      <p class="m-0 border-l-[3px] border-transparent pl-6 text-[19px] leading-[1.65] text-muted-foreground">
        {firstParagraph}
      </p>

      <p class="m-0 border-l-[3px] border-transparent pl-6 text-[19px] leading-[1.65] text-muted-foreground">
        I had a Louis Vuitton-level vision, not the budget. Blender let me build what I could not afford to shoot, but its learning curve is steep.
      </p>

      <p class="m-0 border-l-[3px] border-primary py-1 pl-6 text-[19px] leading-[1.65] text-muted-foreground">
        Cr8-xyz is my attempt to give more creatives access to expert CGI workflows, without starting from zero.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
